  "journal": "J Biomech Eng 101:46-52",
  "doi": "",
  "n": 42,
  "sample": "42 lumbar motion segments from 23 cadavers (16 segments from 10 F, 26 from 13 M); posterior elements removed in the first 18; human cadaver lumbar FSUs L1-L2 to L4-L5 (levels pooled; 3 segments from a Marfan donor, 1 herniated disc), degeneration grade 0-4",
  "age": "21-60 y (mean 43)",
  "sex": "10 F / 13 M donors",
  "height_cm": null,
  "weight_kg": null
 },
 "protocol": {
  "summary": "Single FSUs, vertebrae embedded in epoxy and screwed into fixtures, disc mid-plane horizontal; inferior fixture clamped (rotatable to 0/90/180/270 deg); superior vertebra unconstrained. 400 N compressive preload (vertical strings + pneumatic cylinder) maintained during moments. Moments applied by weights via strings and pulleys on 20 cm arms in >= 3 increments, static, non-repetitive; readings 15 s after each increment (15-25 s to record). Rotations seldom allowed > 8 deg. Motions of the superior vertebral body centre from 6 dial gauges (0.01 mm). IDP by Nachemson needle (membrane-tipped) in the disc, 5 kPa resolution, re-zeroed between sequences. Posterior elements (facets bilaterally, ligamenta flava, inter- and supraspinous ligaments) then removed in the first 18 segments and tests repeated.",
  "how_to_simulate": [
   "Model a lumbar FSU; fix the inferior vertebra; leave the superior vertebra unconstrained",
   "Apply 400 N axial compressive preload (vertical, through the disc centre) and keep it during moment loading",
   "Apply flexion, extension, right/left lateral bending and clockwise torsion moments of 4.7 and 10.6 Nm (static)",
   "Report the principal rotation of the superior vertebra (one direction, from the preloaded position), coupled rotations/translations of its body centre, and nucleus pressure increase above the preloaded pressure"
  ],
  "notes": "Values are means over all segments tested at each load level (n per cell not given; some segments did not reach 10.6 Nm because rotations were limited to ~8 deg); '(a)' cells = 3 specimens. Levels L1-L2 to L4-L5 pooled. Resection: one step only - removal of all posterior-element connections (bilateral facet joints, ligamenta flava, inter- and supraspinous ligaments) in 18 of 42 segments; values are absolute, not % intact, and intact means are over all 42 segments (not paired).",
  "subject_model": null
 },
